    if k == 136 { return "`generation` / `retire` belong to **revision domains**: the domain keeps a counter, `retire` drops an old one and `generation` reads the current one. Other domain kinds have no such counter, so this is not a syntax problem."; }
    if k == 137 { return "`generation` / `retire` 管的是 **revision 域**：域自己记一个代号，`retire` 退掉旧的、`generation` 读当前的。别的域（`disk` / `region` / `session` …）没有那个计数器，所以这不是「改写法」，是「这种域没有这个东西」。"; }
    if k == 138 { return "A capability domain is the one thing Loment adds: `capability c : space[lo..hi]` declares an **index domain** and `guard c(i);` checks that `i` falls inside it (a literal out of range is a **compile-time** error, anything else is a run-time trap). So the domain has to be declared first, `lo <= hi` has to hold, and one name may be declared only once per space."; }
