    if k == 357 { return "`command_main` **不是**被谁直接调用的普通函数 —— 它是工具链生成的那个 `_start` 要去调用的目标，而「生成」这件事只由**命令声明**触发。两半必须成对：没有声明时它是一个**没人调用的函数**（编得过、静默无效）；只有声明而没有它，生成的入口就没有东西可调 —— 那要等到**链接**才炸，所以在检查这一步就拒；签名不对则生成的入口传不进去参数。入口的签名是固定的：`fn command_main(argv: ptr, argc: u32) -> u32`，`argv` 就是 `/proc/self/cmdline` 那一整块，`argv[0]` 是命令自己的路径（`docs/223` §3.2）。"; }
    if k == 358 { return "After codegen that path becomes an **illegal instruction** (`SIGILL`), and it only fires when the path is actually taken - so it is the kind of bug that ships and then blows up when a new input reaches an error branch nobody exercised. \"check passes\" is supposed to mean \"this program will not trap\"; this rule is what makes that true, because a static check is the only place that can say it before the fact."; }
    if k == 359 { return "这类函数发射之后，末尾会落成一条**非法指令**（SIGILL）—— 而它只在**真的走到那一支**时才发生，所以是那种「上线很久、错误分支被新输入踩到」才炸的问题。`check` 通过本该等于「这份程序不会 trap」，这一条就是把那句话兑现：静态检查是唯一能在事前说出口的地方（原先它只是一条写作纪律，见 SKILL.md §6.14）。"; }
    if k == 360 { return "Both numbers here are **known at compile time**, so this is not \"one possible runtime outcome\" - it is **a compile-time fact**, and `docs/205` section 1.1 C5 makes it a language rule: \"an out-of-range access is refused at compile time **when the index is a literal**\". **It does not look at `lms`** (since 2026-10-16, issue #18) - before that date it only fired under `choose lms_open`, and `lms` is a development-channel intermediate that does not ship, so a released user never got it. The same mistake on a capability domain has always been a compile error (`docs/146` section 3); two constructs giving two answers is exactly the inconsistency that issue names. Saying it here is worth it: when it is not refused, clang gets UB (`docs/253` section 4.4 - the IR literally grows a `getelementptr inbounds ... i32 10`) and the in-repo `lomelf` silently writes into the neighbouring bytes."; }
    if k == 361 { return "这里两边的数**都是编译期已知的** —— 所以它不是一个「运行期的一种可能」，而是**一个编译期事实**，`docs/205` §1.1 C5 把这条写成了语言规则：「越界访问在**字面量**时编译期拒」。**它不看 `lms`**（2026-10-16 起，issue #18）—— 在这个日子之前它只在 `choose lms_open` 时发，而 `lms` 是开发通道的中间态、不进发行版，于是发行版的用户拿不到这条。同一件事在`guard` 那一格早就是编译错误（`docs/146` §3），两个构造两个答案正是那个issue 点名的不一致。说死它值当：实测（`docs/253` §4.4）不拒的时候走 clang 是 UB（IR 里直接长出 `getelementptr inbounds … i32 10`），走仓内 `lomelf` 是静默踩相邻字节。"; }
    if k == 362 { return "After `free(p)` that block has gone back to the allocator, so using `p` again is a use-after-free. It **does not necessarily crash** - the block may keep its old bytes until some later `alloc` reuses it (`docs/253` section 5.1), so it is the kind of bug that ships quietly and then blows up when an allocation finally lands on it. The five checks `free` gained in `docs/210` section 2.8 cover **`free`'s own end** (is this really a block, was it already freed); they cannot cover \"used again afterwards\". Separate from E006: moving is an **ownership** matter, freeing is a **legality** one."; }
    if k == 363 { return "`free(p)` 之后那块内存已经还回分配器，再用 `p` 就是 use-after-free。它**不一定会崩** —— 块可能还留着旧字节，一直到最后被下一次 `alloc` 复用（`docs/253` §5.1），所以症状是那种「上线很久、某次分配把它盖掉」才炸的问题。`docs/210` §2.8 给 `free` 加的那五条检查管的是 **`free` 自己那一端**（是不是真块、有没有重复释放），管不了「之后再用」。与 E006 分开：移走是**所有权**的事，释放是**合法性**的事。"; }
    if k == 364 { return "Loment's type table is **fixed**: `u8`..`u64`, `i8`..`i64`, `bool`, `ptr`, `str`, `()`, plus the `struct` / `enum` you declare and arrays/slices of those - no generic containers, and **no floating point** (`loment types` prints the whole list). So this is not \"that name was not declared\"; it is \"**this language has no such type**\". That is also why it is separate from E002: E002 is fixed by declaring the name, this one by naming a type that exists."; }
    if k == 365 { return "Loment 的类型表是**固定的**：`u8`..`u64`、`i8`..`i64`、`bool`、`ptr`、`str`、`()`，加上你声明的 `struct` / `enum` 与它们的数组/切片 —— 没有泛型容器，**也没有浮点**（`loment types` 打出来就是全部）。所以这一条说的不是\"这个名字没声明\"，而是\"**这门语言没有这种类型**\"。它与 E002 分开的理由也在这里：E002 的修法是声明那个名字，这一条的修法是换一个真有的类型。"; }
